The CPU backend offers its nodes to stable-diffusion.assembly with the nodes after them

The loop of a graph over its nodes calls sdasm_compute_nodes() first, with the graph's nodes, as the graph holds them, their number and the index of the node, which computes the node with stable-diffusion.assembly's kernels when they take it -- along with the nodes after it that change its output in place, element by element, the bias of a convolution or of a linear layer, the scale, the shift and the SiLU after a normalisation -- and says how many nodes of the graph that was, or 0, on every thread alike, when the kernels do not take the node. The loop then goes on past those nodes, or computes the node as it would have. A graph planned for the reference implementation (use_ref) is not offered.

The function is stable-diffusion.assembly's, declared by its header, which patch 0001 includes.

This is stable-diffusion.assembly's own patch, applied to the submodule by cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, after patch 0002; it is not for upstream. ggml's part is under the MIT License, and the patch's under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or any later version.

diff --git a/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c b/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
--- a/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
+++ b/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
@@ -3334,13 +3334,21 @@
 
         const uint64_t node_start = profiling ? sdasm_profile_now() : 0;
 
-        // TODO: move fused-op detection into ggml_graph_plan so fusion decisions are made once at planning time
-        // Try fused ops, fall back to normal compute
-        const int n_fused = ggml_cpu_try_fuse_ops(cgraph, node_n, &params, cplan);
-        if (n_fused > 0) {
+        // stable-diffusion.assembly computes the node, with the nodes after it
+        // that change its output in place, when it takes it.
+        const int n_taken = cplan->use_ref ? 0 : sdasm_compute_nodes(&params, cgraph->nodes, cgraph->n_nodes, node_n);
+        int n_fused = n_taken - 1;
+        if (n_taken > 0) {
             node_n += n_fused;
         } else {
-            ggml_compute_forward(&params, node);
+            // TODO: move fused-op detection into ggml_graph_plan so fusion decisions are made once at planning time
+            // Try fused ops, fall back to normal compute
+            n_fused = ggml_cpu_try_fuse_ops(cgraph, node_n, &params, cplan);
+            if (n_fused > 0) {
+                node_n += n_fused;
+            } else {
+                ggml_compute_forward(&params, node);
+            }
         }
 
